%[text] %[text:anchor:H_232a] ### **Characterization of linear system solutions in terms of matrices**
%[text] An important feature of the matrix representation is that it allows you to quickly compute whether a system of equations has a unique solution. Consider a linear system with $n${"altText":"n"} equations and $n${"altText":"n"} unknowns. It can be represented in matrix form as
%[text]{"align":"center"}  $\\mathbf{Ax} = \\mathbf{b}${"altText":"Ax=b"}
%[text] For this system, the following are equivalent (this is part of the **Invertible Matrix Theorem**):
%[text] - $\\mathbf{A}${"altText":"A"} is invertible
%[text] - $|\\mathbf{A}|${"altText":"|A|"} is nonzero
%[text] - The linear system has a unique solution for every $\\mathbf{b}${"altText":"b"} in $\\mathbb{R}^n${"altText":"R^n"}. \
%[text] If you want to check if a system has a unique solution, you can represent the system in matrix form, and then compute $|\\mathbf{A}|${"altText":"|A|"}. If the determinant is nonzero, the system has a unique solution for any $\\mathbf{b}${"altText":"b"}.
%[text] ![](text:image:0470) **Exercise**. Determine if the systems have a unique solution by (1) writing the system in matrix form and (2) computing the determinant of the coefficient matrix.
%[text] (a)  $\\begin{array}{r}\n2x +y = 2\n\\\\ \nx - y  = 10\n\\end{array}${"altText":"system of equations: 2x +y = 2 ; x - y = 10"} 
ShowSolutionA = false; %[control:checkbox:38bf]{"position":[17,22]}
syms x y z
A = sym([2 1; 1 -1]);
b = sym([2; 10]);
xvec = [x; y];
if(ShowSolutionA)
    displayFormula([char(A),char(xvec),"' = '",char(b)]);
    disp("|A| = " + string(det(A)) + " which is nonzero. This implies that the system has a unique solution.")
end
%%
%[text] (b) $\\begin{array}{r}\n2x +y + 4z = 2\n\\\\ \nx - z = 10\n\\\\ \n-3x + 2 y - z = 11\n\\end{array}${"altText":"system of equations: 2x +y + 4z = 2 ; x - z = 10 ; -3x + 2 y - z = 11"} 
ShowSolutionB = false; %[control:checkbox:5aff]{"position":[17,22]}
A = sym([2 1 4; 1 0 -1; -3 2 -1]);
b = sym([2; 10; 11]);
xvec = [x; y; z];
if(ShowSolutionB)
    displayFormula([char(A),char(xvec),"' = '",char(b)]);
    disp("|A| = " + string(det(A)) + " which is nonzero. This implies that the system has a unique solution.")
end
